@SYSTEM_TITLE
; Emuera reads `p`/`P` as a base-2 exponent and `e`/`E` as a base-10 one after
; any significand, evaluates `significand * pow(base, exponent)` in `double`
; and range-checks it against Int64 (`Sub/LexicalAnalyzer.cs:172-190`).
PRINTFORML {1P31}
PRINTFORML {1p31}
; The significand multiplies the power, so `2P16` is 2 * 2^16.
PRINTFORML {2P16}
PRINTFORML {3E4}
PRINTFORML {3e4}
; An exponent of zero leaves the significand alone instead of going through
; `double`, so a value `double` cannot hold exactly still survives.
PRINTFORML {1P0}
PRINTFORML {9007199254740993P0}
; `1P63` passes Emuera's `d > Int64.MaxValue` check, because the comparison
; promotes `Int64.MaxValue` to 2^63, and then reaches the *unchecked*
; `(Int64)d` cast, which yields `long.MinValue`.
PRINTFORML {1P63}
